# C037 (x-suluk-store + x-suluk-notify) — the REACTIVE-CLIENT facet. The contract's statement of how the frontend
# should turn operations into reactive STATE (a query backs a `$<key>` store), EVENTS (a mutation invalidates stores
# on success), and CALLBACKS (a 2xx success message + a doc-level status->severity notify policy) — so @suluk/sdk can
# GENERATE a ready-to-use reactive client instead of every consumer hand-wiring nanostores + invalidation + a toast
# policy (the exact boilerplate observed in toolfactory: stores/session.ts + lib/api-toast.ts + a per-panel load()).
# Operator-directed (toolfactory session 2026-06-26). Spec-first: this Step RATIFIES the facet; the @suluk/sdk reactive
# CODEGEN + the nanostores runtime adapter are the deferred follow-on. ORIGINATED + generator-not-yet-built ⇒ the
# DESIGN claims carry an honestly LOW ceiling; only the client-only SAFETY claim is higher (it is trivially witnessed).

# CLIENT-CODEGEN ONLY (the load-bearing safety property; STRONGER than every prior facet's D1 claim). x-suluk-store is a
# per-op Request facet; x-suluk-notify is a doc-level sibling. NEITHER is read by ANY server path: not buildAda, not
# matchRequest, not the runtime-advisory agent/job/policy selection. The other x-suluk-* facets at least feed
# runtime-advisory selection; this one feeds ONLY the @suluk/sdk frontend generator. So the request->operation matcher
# is invariant to it, AND it has zero server-side effect at all. WITNESS (independent of the code-reading):
# test/store-d1-invariance.test.ts asserts buildAda(docWithStore+notify) deep-equals buildAda(docWithout) and
# matchRequest resolves every op identically. A store/notify-stripped doc yields a BYTE-IDENTICAL Ada.
claim d1_store_selector_safe: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when d1_store_selector_safe == False

# NO REQUEST-VALUE SELECTOR. Every field of SulukStore / SulukNotifyPolicy names an author-chosen STORE NAME
# (key/invalidates), a PARAM NAME (params — names, never values), a config scalar (ttl/revalidateOnFocus), an advisory
# message (onSuccess), or an HTTP status / status-class / "network" (the notify keys). NONE references a request, DOM,
# header, body, or query VALUE — so nothing here can leak into a matcher selector even if a future reader consulted it
# (the same wall C018 puts around callback keys and C024 around the event-expression attribution).
claim store_no_request_value_selector: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when store_no_request_value_selector == False

# DISJOINT QUERY / MUTATION ROLES (the discriminator, mirroring C027's presence-of-model). A SulukStore plays ONE of
# two roles: a QUERY (presence of `key`) projects to a `$<key>` reactive store; a MUTATION (presence of `invalidates`)
# invalidates named stores on a 2xx. presence-of-`key` discriminates the role exactly as presence-of-`model`
# discriminates skill-vs-route in C027 — a future lint flags an op declaring both. The states/events split the operator
# asked for maps onto key/invalidates; the callbacks split maps onto onSuccess (success) + x-suluk-notify (status policy).
claim store_query_mutation_disjoint_roles: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when store_query_mutation_disjoint_roles == False

# TARGET-AGNOSTIC SEAM (rides C034 one layer up). The facet declares a dependency GRAPH (which queries back stores;
# which mutations invalidate which stores) + cache hints + a status->severity policy — NOT a nanostores program. The
# @suluk/sdk default adapter projects it to nanostores + @nanostores/query (peer deps, same bring-your-own model as
# ofetch), but a different adapter could project to TanStack Query / SWR / Pinia Colada; the notify policy projects to
# an INJECTED notify(severity, problem) renderer (policy declared, rendering injected). This is the C034
# runtime-adapter-seam move (one declaration -> many targets) applied to the reactive client. ORIGINATED application
# of a 0.85 precedent ⇒ low ceiling here.
claim store_target_agnostic_seam: Bool @>=0.45 = True
falsified_when store_target_agnostic_seam == False

# STRUCTURAL-ONLY + ORIGINATED, RIDES C025/C027/C036 EXACTLY. x-suluk-notify is a doc-level x-* sibling (legal under
# the document's `[ext: x-${string}]` catch-all); x-suluk-store is an explicit Request facet beside the shipped
# x-suluk-ratelimit / x-suluk-approval. OPTIONAL, additive, NO new normative kind, NO meta-schema change; a pre-C037 doc
# and a store/notify-bearing one validate byte-identically; a 3.1 downgrade drops both facets whole and the operations
# survive unchanged. Types added to core/src/types.ts (SulukStore / SulukNotifyPolicy / SulukNotifySeverity,
# structural-only) + re-exported. Honest ceiling: the GENERATOR + the nanostores runtime are NOT built in this Step
# (spec-first per operator), so the design is unwitnessed by a real projection ⇒ ceiling <=0.5. Recorded as a daftar
# burhan.segment receipt (operator-surfaced-cowpath, same pattern as C027/C036).
claim store_facet_structural_originated: Bool @>=0.45 = True
falsified_when store_facet_structural_originated == False
